    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:00Z",
      "text": "At least 24 dead after boat taking passengers to funeral capsizes in Nigeria, Sky News reports.",
      "cites": [
        "news:sky:46338f879cf9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "Also reported by DW.",
      "cites": [
        "news:dw:a7e001c6016b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:17Z",
      "text": "Inflation in Nigeria was 23.0% in 2025, down from 33.2% in 2024.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG:NG"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:26Z",
      "text": "The economy grew 4.0% in 2025; unemployment stood at 3.1%.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG:NG",
        "wb:SL.UEM.TOTL.ZS:NG"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:35Z",
      "text": "Across Sub-Saharan Africa, Nigeria's 23.0% compares with a median of 3.5%; the highest is South Sudan at 91.4%.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG:region:sub-saharan-africa"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "Nigeria, officially the Federal Republic of Nigeria, is a country in West Africa between the Sahel to the north and the Gulf of Guinea in the Atlantic Ocean to the south.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385888850:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:01:00Z",
